erstands complicated technology\", \"Excellent attention skills\". So we have that evidence: C is calm in crisis, technical competence, attention. So C is strong across many criteria, but communication issues.\n\nB: we have no evidence of calm in crisis, but handles stress well. So B is also stress resilient.\n\nNow we need to decide. The panel hasn't fully discussed A, but we know lack of reliability and stress evidence. So A is weak.\n\nWe need to make a contribution: perhaps we can argue that while D and C have strong points, B's conscientiousness and stress handling, plus technical competence, outweigh the communication issues, which could be mitigated. Or we could shift to C. Let's see: B's communication issues are severe: nasty remarks, pretentious, wrong tone. That could be dangerous. D's hot temper also dangerous. C's communication difficulty and egocentric may be less severe? Hard to say. C also has 100% reliability and quick decisions, positive crew atmosphere, calm in crisis, excellent attention. That seems strongest overall. So perhaps we should shift our vote to C, aligning with Agent 1. That would bring consensus.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: mention that Agent 1 highlighted C's reliability and decision making, and that we now see C also has calmness and technical competence (from shared mental model). We can argue that C's communication issues are less severe than B's nasty remarks and D's hot temper. So we change vote to C.\n\nThus our public message: I agree with Agent 1 that C's reliability and quick correct decisions, plus calmness in crisis and excellent attention, make C the strongest overall fit. I shift my vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: 100% reliability, makes correct decisions quickly, creates positive crew atmosphere, keeps calm in crisis, excellent attention skills. Also mention concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, but these are manageable.\n\nThus metadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
